course: dictionary
lesson: 5019
title: Influenza and flu
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Influenza is a long word for an illness caused by a virus. People shorten it to flu. The context tells you what it means: «Flu is caused by influenza viruses and is much worse than a cold.» Because it is caused by a virus, it is not just a bit of a cold.
explain: Read the clues around the word. The sentence says flu «comes on suddenly, with high fever and aching all over.» Those clues show that flu is a serious illness that starts quickly and makes your whole body feel bad.
explain: The sentence also compares flu to being «hit by a bus». This is an exaggeration, a way of showing how bad you feel. It does not mean a bus has hit you. Always check whether a comparison is meant to be taken literally.
fact: Influenza means an illness caused by a virus, with a high temperature, aches, a sore throat, a cough and great tiredness.
fact: People often shorten influenza to «flu» in everyday speech.
fact: Flu is caused by a virus, so antibiotics do not work on it.
fact: Vaccines help protect people from flu, and a flu jab is one way to get that protection.
fact: Flu spreads easily from person to person, which is why flu season is a busy time for doctors.
exercise: «Flu is caused by influenza viruses and is much worse than a cold.» What is influenza? | A kind of cold drink | A type of bacteria that antibiotics kill | A large bird that lives near water | *An illness caused by a virus, with a high temperature and aches
exercise: Sam says flu is just a bad cold. Which words from the sentence show that flu is worse? | It is a kind of food | It only makes your nose run | *It comes on suddenly, with high fever and aching all over | It is much smaller than a cold
exercise: Which is the short form of influenza that people often use? | cold | *flu | fizz | influence
test: Why do antibiotics not work on flu? | Because flu is too big to be treated | Because flu is caused by too much sunshine | Because antibiotics only work in summer | *Because flu is caused by a virus, not bacteria
test: What is a flu jab for? | To help you read faster | *To help protect you from flu | To cure a broken arm | To make you hot and sweaty
exam: In «Flu ... comes on suddenly, with high fever», which one word tells you how quickly flu starts? | cold | *suddenly | bus | much
